            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Qu?n Du? is a Chinese Rummy-like draw-and-discard game from Dongguan, Guangdong. Players collect a 16-card hand of eight pairs, with identical pairs able to claim priority from the discard.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: China (Dongguan, Guangdong province). The game uses Dongguan Pai (Chinese money cards). Rules were recorded from observations of games between Chinese players in Amsterdam. Cultural Significance: Social card game in Chinese communities.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
